# Salmon with Dijon Mustard Sauce

Based on [https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/…](https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/219911/chef-johns-salmon) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20241127051330/https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/219911/chef-johns-salmon))

{ rating="4" image="salmon_with_dijon_mustard_sauce.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 lb [Salmon Filet]{ ing="salmon-filet" } with skin
- [ ] 1 clove [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, sliced
- [ ] 1.5 Tbsp [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp fresh [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [basil]{ ing="basil" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [thyme]{ ing="thyme" }
- [ ] pinch of [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] pinch [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }

## Recipe

1. Combine sauce in a small bowl and mix
1. Preheat oven to 400
1. Place on tin foil and fold up the sides
1. Bake for 10-12 minutes until internal temperature of 120-130

## Notes

1. Recipe has mostly been cut in half to reduce the volume of the sauce and reduce the proportion of Dijon mustard
